    "round-trip judge left implication translation_implies_source unclear",
    "round-trip judge left implication source_implies_translation unclear"
  ],
  "resolved_items": [
    {
      "item": "direct judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "The construction preserves the selected spectral Riemann problem. Its additional conclusions impose no extra premises on the source matrices or states. However, the supplied evidence does not fully establish the measure semantics needed to certify the analytic conjunct.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed pages 1, 3, and 5–6; target quantifiers; definitions D001–D006; D080 supplies only inferInstance."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "The concern about identifying the selected measure is an evidence gap, not a demonstrated wrong-measure implementation. The direct judge's identification as Lebesgue measure is not independently supported by an expanded instance or identifying theorem in the permitted evidence.",
      "primary_evidence": "D080 has type MeasureTheory.MeasureSpace Real and body inferInstance. D067 merely projects that structure's measure. The reuse ledger contains no interpretation establishing D080."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge classification is undetermined",
      "resolution": "Retain undetermined. The favorable algebraic and geometric findings do not settle the unresolved analytic dependency or justify a definitive reverse implication.",
      "primary_evidence": "D001 supplies the complete real eigenbasis; D003–D006 supply the spectral waves; D002 uses the unresolved D080 measure in every integral."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge classification is undetermined",
      "resolution": "Retain undetermined on evidence grounds. No actual counterexample to the target's faithfulness has been established, so a negative faithfulness classification would also be unsupported.",
      "primary_evidence": "The blind translation agrees with the supplied target and D001–D006. Its D080 ambiguity remains present in both complete declaration dossiers."
    },
    {
      "item": "blind translator left dependency_coverage item D080 unclear",
      "resolution": "The uncertainty cannot be eliminated from the supplied declaration. Exact normalization alone is unnecessary: replacing Lebesgue measure by a common positive finite multiple scales both sides of D002 equally and preserves interval integrability. What remains necessary is evidence identifying the measure sufficiently to exclude a degenerate or otherwise incompatible measure.",
      "primary_evidence": "D080: MeasureTheory.MeasureSpace Real := inferInstance. D067 projects its measure. D002 uses that same measure for spatial and temporal integrals; D065 and D089 expose integrability and oriented integration without identifying the measure."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C07 unclear",
      "resolution": "The exact construction and positive-time similarity do not contradict the source's qualified general discussion. The theorem concerns linear systems only. Nevertheless, the selected pages do not alone specify the full pointwise representative and all-real-time analytic assertion, so equivalence versus genuine additional strength remains unresolved.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 5 qualifies the general similarity description and then separately asserts linear spectral solvability. D003 fixes the representative; D002 quantifies over all real times; the target restricts similarity to t > 0."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C10 unclear",
      "resolution": "No reduced applicability is present. Finite indexing includes every source dimension, the empty type adds a degenerate case, and all-real-time conservation extends the conclusion rather than restricting the hypotheses. These observations settle the applicability issue but do not by themselves prove strict strengthening.",
      "primary_evidence": "The target universally quantifies an arbitrary Fintype and all three states. D001 has no distinctness or nonzero-speed premise. D002 has unrestricted real temporal endpoints."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C05 unclear",
      "resolution": "All required structural conclusions are represented: spectral construction, finite waves at eigenvalue speeds, initial half-line data, and positive-time similarity. The conservation conjunct has the correct balance form, but its interpretation as ordinary integral conservation remains conditional on resolving D080.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed pages 3 and 5–6; D003 sums over Finset.univ using D005–D006; D004 supplies the initial branches; D002 asserts terminal-minus-initial spatial integral equals integrated left-minus-right flux."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C06 unclear",
      "resolution": "Rechecking the disputed dependency chain confirms that matrix multiplication, basis coordinates, profile translation, subtraction orientation, and interval integrability have the stated roles. The remaining operator uncertainty is the selected measure, not these algebraic operations. Reuse hashes do not establish that missing meaning.",
      "primary_evidence": "D022 is row-wise matrix action; D024 reconstructs basis vectors; D068 extracts basis coordinates; D006 uses x − speed*t; D065 requires integrability on both endpoint orientations; D089 defines the oriented integral; D080 remains unexpanded."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C07 unclear",
      "resolution": "Exact equality is appropriate for the constructed solution, and the finite-wave formula supports unconditional similarity in this linear setting. A binary strength classification is still unavailable because the analytic dependency and the reverse implication remain unsettled.",
      "primary_evidence": "The target's equalities concern the same D003 function throughout. For t > 0, x − λ*t and x/t − λ have identical signs and vanish together, preserving every D004 branch."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C11 unclear",
      "resolution": "The origin and characteristic-line choices are compatible with ordinary Lebesgue conservation. Changing the origin state changes each spatial slice at finitely many points. A moving mode changes a fixed temporal slice at at most one time; a stationary mode may change it for all times at x = 0, but its flux contribution vanishes because its eigenvalue is zero. Thus stationary fronts do not invalidate the construction. Applying this argument to the actual integral instance remains conditional on D080.",
      "primary_evidence": "Equation (1.11) leaves x = 0 unspecified. D003–D006 transport the coordinates of the arbitrary origin state on x = λ_p*t. The eigenvector conjunct gives A e_p = λ_p e_p, including zero eigenvalues."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C12 unclear",
      "resolution": "The hypotheses and spectral construction are nonvacuous in positive dimension. A singleton index, A = 1, standard basis, and distinct left and right states give a moving nonconstant step. Explicit integrability excludes reliance on default integrals of nonintegrable functions. Analytic nondegeneracy of the encoded balance is not established solely by that example while D080 remains unidentified.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 1 includes real scalar advection. D001 admits the scalar identity matrix; D003 becomes a profile translated by t. D002 explicitly requires sectionwise interval integrability, but D080's displayed type does not assert a nonzero measure."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear",
      "resolution": "Spectral completeness, solution existence, and the absence of an unsupported PDE uniqueness claim are confirmed. No matrix invertibility or classical differentiability at jumps is required. Certification of the analytic solution predicate remains conditional on its measure semantics.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 3 requires independent complete eigenvectors and states unique vector decomposition. The target existentially supplies spectral witnesses and solution properties, with no uniqueness quantifier. D002 is integral rather than differential."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left implication source_implies_lean unclear",
      "resolution": "Retain unclear. Absence of an explicit formula on the selected pages is not a counterexample to implication. Conversely, compatibility of the formula does not alone establish that the source claim entails every quantified analytic and representative refinement. The unresolved measure prevents completing that comparison.",
      "primary_evidence": "The sentence crossing printed pages 5–6 defers the construction to Chapter 3. D002–D004 add a specified representative and conservation for all real temporal endpoints, using D080."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication translation_implies_source unclear",
      "resolution": "The translation accurately reconstructs the supplied declaration. Conditional on ordinary nondegenerate Lebesgue measure semantics, its conserved spectral construction establishes the selected source result. That condition is not established by the supplied D080 evidence, so the analytic implication cannot be certified without qualification.",
      "primary_evidence": "Blind translation definitions match D001–D006, D022, D068, D065, and D089. Printed page 5 explicitly retains integral conservation at discontinuities. D080 does not expose the selected instance."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication source_implies_translation unclear",
      "resolution": "Retain unclear for the same reasons as source_implies_lean: the translation adds no independent semantic discrepancy, but the exact analytic instance and status of the additional quantified construction properties remain unresolved.",
      "primary_evidence": "The blind translation states the same finite spectral formula, all-real-time rectangle identity, arbitrary origin parameter, and positive-time similarity as the target and its definitions."
    }
  ],
  "implications": {
    "lean_implies_source": {
      "verdict": "unclear",
      "reasoning": "The real hyperbolicity assumption, arbitrary source states, complete eigenvector decomposition, finite eigenvalue-speed waves, initial half-line assignments, and positive-time similarity match. With ordinary Lebesgue measure, D002 supplies the required integral conservation, including at discontinuities, and the explicit function is locally constant away from characteristic lines. However, D080 is presented only as inferInstance; neither its expanded instance nor a measure-identification theorem is supplied. The direct judge's unconditional analytic identification therefore exceeds the available declaration evidence. This is an unresolved evidentiary condition, not proof that the implementation uses an incorrect measure."
    },
    "source_implies_lean": {
      "verdict": "unclear",
      "reasoning": "The source supports spectral solvability and the accompanying wave structure, but the selected pages defer the construction and do not explicitly formulate the target's representative choices or conservation for every pair of real times. Those choices are compatible with the intended linear problem and do not reduce applicability. Their absence from the printed formulation does not establish nonimplication, while their plausibility does not establish equivalence or strict strength. Together with the unresolved actual measure instance, this prevents a definitive reverse implication."
    }
  },
  "classification": "undetermined",
  "accepted": false,
  "remaining_uncertainties": [
    "The permitted inline evidence does not identify the instance selected by D080 sufficiently to establish ordinary nondegenerate Lebesgue integration. Its exact normalization is not essential when both sides use the same positive finite scaling.",
    "The reverse implication has not been established for the complete target, including its specified spectral representative and all-real-time conservation assertion. No counterexample establishing strict nonimplication has been supplied or derived."
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "dependency-evidence-gap",
      "evidence": "D080 has body inferInstance in the direct packet, complete inventory, and blind dossier. D067 only projects the selected measure. No supplied reuse record or identifying declaration closes this gap.",
      "impact": "The central conservation predicate cannot be unconditionally identified with the source's ordinary integral conservation from the permitted evidence. This is a limitation of the audit evidence, not a demonstrated defect in the Lean theorem."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "boundary-convention-resolved-conditionally",
      "evidence": "D003 transports origin-state coordinates only on their characteristic lines. Moving-line changes are isolated in temporal slices; stationary eigenmodes have zero contribution to A q.",
      "impact": "Arbitrary origin values do not obstruct rectangle conservation under ordinary Lebesgue semantics, including rectangles whose boundary coincides with a stationary front."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "applicability-and-strength",
      "evidence": "The target has no added distinctness, nonzero-speed, invertibility, orthogonality, or regularity premises. It admits all finite source dimensions and arbitrary states; D002 extends temporal conclusion scope.",
      "impact": "No purported strength arises from reduced applicability. Additional precision alone nevertheless does not establish a strict implication difference."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "Independent inspection of the attached primary-source images and the inline declaration evidence confirms the intended spectral construction and resolves the substantive boundary and applicability concerns. The blind translation accurately reflects the target. The remaining measure-identification gap cannot be closed by declaration names, module provenance, a reuse hash, or agreement between judges. Because the permitted evidence does not settle both implication directions, undetermined with acceptance withheld is the consistent outcome. No tools, target proof, external context, or independent hash recomputation were used."
}
